EXTENSION "ARMDef_Faith_and_Flame_TheCountyOfToulouse_AdamCarpentiereFollowerOfVerditiusWhiteFaction" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Faith & Flame - Adam Carpentiere, Follower of Verditius, White Faction"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_Faith_and_Flame_Core_Ext"

    # Adam Carpentiere, Follower of Verditius, White Faction (Chapter Four: The County of Toulouse, p41): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #tb98276e2fa1a599a2fccf3 ^"Adam Carpentiere, Follower of Verditius, White Faction" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#tea3c2372bb55a06d9a8c83 ^"Tolosa Paratge"]
            ^"Age" STRING "77 (Apparent age: 65)"
            ^"Personality Trait" STRING "Industrious +3, Hubris +3, Avaricious +2"
            ^"Source" STRING "Faith & Flame"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 41
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Adam has long maintained a sanctum and laboratory within the city, located in a waterfront lacuna with a Magic aura of 2. He is far more involved in city politics than the politics of his home covenant. He has joined the White faction owing only to his deep seated anti-Semitism, for he owes a substantial sum to the Jewish moneylenders of Cahors, and therefore Bishop Foulque’s anti-Semitic and anti-Cathar rhetoric appeals to him. His plans for the enchanted boom across the river to help maintain the regio were resisted by the Gorgiastics, who felt it might adversely effect the aura, and he has never forgotten. Following the Wizard’s Wars he has therefore sided with St. Tropez, whom he regards as representing the best interests of the covenant. Adam is deeply immersed in the magic of Hermetic Architecture (see *The Mysteries Revised Edition,* page 97)"
    }

}
